From 871779cedaedacff527397b411be27e249318b26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:45:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] chronik: native index tables (blocks, txs, block stats,
 spent-by) and DB dump

Port chronik-db io/{blocks,txs,block_stats,spent_by,merge}.rs,
reverse_lookup.rs, index_tx.rs and data.rs on top of the KvStore
interface, with the same key/value encodings as Rust schema v13 so
native and Rust share one database. The merge-operator emulation is an
explicit read-modify-write with the Rust error texts.

Also add the DB dump used by the parity tooling: every table as sorted
"table<TAB>key_hex<TAB>value_hex" lines with dup values expanded.

Tests: every Rust #[test] of these modules (8) plus index_tx and dump
cases.

Tier: eCash
